From e76c4552072ed59012d4f5839dcb5665054f59c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Otavio Salvador <otavio@ossystems.com.br>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 03:01:10 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] feat(server): Git hooks start with the project's direnv
 environment

Commits and pushes from T3 Code ran Git with the server's own environment, so hooks that call
tools only the project's .envrc provides, such as pnpm from a Nix dev shell, failed and the push
reported only a non-zero Git exit.

Commit and push now get the same approved direnv environment as the agent, resolved from the
thread, the project, or the workspace root, and publishing a repository pushes with it too. An
unapproved or failing .envrc runs Git without it, as before.
